Wrong (B): Both losses and expenses are recognized on the accrual basis under GAAP; the cash-versus-accrual distinction does not differentiate these elements.
Wrong (C): Both losses and expenses can reduce assets or increase liabilities; the direction of the balance sheet effect does not distinguish them.
