-- Q12221: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 450-20-25-2, a loss contingency is recognized only when the loss is both probable (generally interpreted as >75%) and reasonably estimable. At 40%, the loss is reasonably possible but not probable, so ASC 450-20-50-3 requires footnote disclosure rather than recognition.
Wrong (A): Environmental obligations do not automatically meet the probable threshold; the 40% probability must be evaluated against ASC 450''s recognition criteria.
Wrong (B): At 40%, the loss is reasonably possible (more than remote), so disclosure is required under ASC 450-20-50-3 even though recognition is not.
Wrong (C): While the Conceptual Framework''s liability definition does not require probability thresholds, ASC 450''s specific recognition criteria control, and the framework is nonauthoritative.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12221;

