-- Q12224: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8 Chapter 3 (ASC 105), recognition requires that an item meets an element definition and can be measured with sufficient faithful representation. When measurement uncertainty is extreme -- a $2M to $8M range with unresolved regulatory outcomes -- any point estimate would lack sufficient reliability to be useful to decision-makers.
Wrong (B): The $2,000,000 conservative estimate reflects conservatism bias, not faithful representation; prudence alone does not justify recognition under extreme uncertainty.
Wrong (C): Recognizing the maximum $8,000,000 would sacrifice faithful representation for completeness, overstating the asset''s likely value.
Wrong (D): The midpoint of $5,000,000 appears neutral, but neutrality alone does not overcome the problem that the wide range makes any single estimate potentially misleading.$EXPL$
