-- Q12233: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 105-10-05-1, the Codification is the sole source of authoritative GAAP. FASB Concepts Statements are explicitly nonauthoritative -- they inform standard-setting but do not establish recognition requirements. ASC 350-20-25-3 prohibits capitalizing internally generated goodwill, and this specific prohibition controls.
Wrong (A): The Conceptual Framework does not take precedence over the Codification; it is nonauthoritative guidance used by the Board in developing standards, not by preparers in applying them.
Wrong (B): Internally generated goodwill arguably does meet the broad asset definition, but the prohibition is based on ASC 350''s specific guidance, not a definitional failure.
Wrong (C): Meeting an element definition does not automatically require recognition; specific Codification guidance may prohibit recognition even when the definition is satisfied.$EXPL$
