UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 235-10-50 and SFAC No. 8, the full disclosure principle requires financial statements to include all information significant enough to influence an informed user''s economic decisions, including notes, supplementary schedules, and parenthetical disclosures.
Wrong (B): Full disclosure does not require revealing proprietary strategies; it covers financial information material to decision-making, not competitive intelligence.
Wrong (C): Disclosure is driven by qualitative materiality and user needs, not by arbitrary dollar thresholds applied to individual transactions.
