-- Q12237: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 105 and SSARS, cash-basis statements are a special purpose framework suitable for users who contractually agree to receive non-GAAP information, such as a lender under a loan covenant. General-purpose investors evaluating equity need GAAP-basis statements with accrual information about receivables, payables, and deferred items.
Wrong (A): Users cannot reliably derive full accrual information from cash flow data alone; material timing differences between cash and accrual amounts would be obscured.
Wrong (C): Cash-basis and accrual-basis statements do not contain identical information; cash basis omits receivables, payables, deferrals, and accruals that equity investors need.
Wrong (D): SFAC No. 8 distinguishes between general-purpose and special-purpose frameworks, and cash basis does not meet general-purpose financial reporting objectives.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12237;

