  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under SFAC No. 8 (ASC 250), consistency requires the same accounting methods be applied to similar transactions from period to period within the same entity. Consistency contributes to comparability by enabling users to identify trends over time.
Wrong (A): Timeliness relates to making information available to decision-makers early enough to influence their decisions, not to method uniformity.
Wrong (B): Verifiability means that knowledgeable independent observers could reach consensus that a representation is faithful, not that the same methods are used over time.
Wrong (C): Understandability means presenting information clearly so that reasonably informed users can comprehend it, not applying uniform methods across periods.$EXPL$
