Wrong (B): $112,500 results from computing tax on the combined total of all components ($450,000 x 25%), violating the separate-component allocation principle of intraperiod allocation.
Wrong (C): $100,000 appears to tax only the net of continuing operations and discontinued operations ($400,000 x 25%), incorrectly netting components before allocation.
