-- Q12272: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 505-20-30-3, a small stock dividend (less than 20-25% of outstanding shares) transfers fair market value from retained earnings to common stock and additional paid-in capital. This reclassifies $150,000 within equity rather than distributing assets, so total stockholders'' equity remains unchanged.
Wrong (A): A stock dividend does not transfer assets to shareholders and therefore does not reduce total equity; it merely reclassifies amounts within equity accounts.
Wrong (B): Total stockholders'' equity cannot increase from a stock dividend because no new resources are received by the entity; the entry is entirely within equity.
Wrong (D): $10,000 equals par value of the new shares (10,000 x $1), but this amount is reclassified within equity, not removed from it.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12272;

-- Q12276: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 205-30-25, when liquidation is imminent, the entity adopts the liquidation basis. Assets are measured at the amount expected to be collected upon disposal (the land at $3.5 million), and the entity must accrue estimated disposal costs and remaining operating costs ($400,000) as liabilities.
Wrong (B): Historical cost is abandoned under the liquidation basis; assets are remeasured to estimated disposal values, not retained at carrying amounts.
Wrong (C): Net realizable value is not the prescribed measurement; ASC 205-30 requires estimated disposal values. Additionally, expected costs must be accrued immediately, not deferred until paid.
Wrong (D): ASC 820 fair value is not the prescribed measurement under liquidation basis; estimated disposal values may differ from fair value, and liabilities must also be adjusted.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12276;
